The split agreed at v3 was never filed: v4 built child A (engine + table) inside the #197
parent bundle, still 173 KB against the 100 KB backstop. In Plan, run
`nl-shell-pdca split 197` then `--accept` so child A/B/C become their own issues and bundles;
do not rebuild #197 as a whole.
Carry into child A's brief as regressions (all in-class bypasses found in v4):
- ANSI-C NUL truncation: `$'sudo\0ignored' -i` must be rejected, and `$'rm\0ignored' -rf build`
  must be destructive (bash cuts at the NUL; the decoder marks the word nonliteral and skips lookup).
  Also `foo $'sudo\0ignored'` (decision A).
- Elevation must reach inner commands: `sudo bash $x`, `sudo env $x bash`, `sudo nice $x bash`,
  `sudo xargs -o bash`, `sudo busybox --pdca` rejected as proposals (an unreadable word or
  undeclared option under an elevating row rejects).
- `script` needs a row (no command opens $SHELL; `-c` is runs-text bash): `sudo script` rejected.
- xargs replace strings (`-I%`, `-i`, `--replace=@`) may become options at run time:
  `xargs -I% sudo % true`, `xargs -o -I% sudo %` rejected; `xargs -I% git reset %`,
  `xargs -I% chown % bob /` at least destructive. Add these tests.
